# This Pim's variables: copy to /etc/pim/pim.env and pass it to deploy.sh as --vars. Nothing
# here is secret; secrets go in secrets.env. Each is a variable in docs/reference.md's Deploy
# table, with its default in src/deployment.ts; leave a line out for the default. A change takes
# a deploy.sh run (there is no dashboard): nodes adopt the new deployment within 30 seconds.
# Format: NAME=value, bare: no quotes, spaces, backslashes, $ or # in a value (docs/celld.md, Variables and secrets).

# Required. The address people use, served by the TLS proxy (caddy/Caddyfile). Passkeys belong
# to its hostname, so choose the one you'll keep before anyone joins.
PIM_PUBLIC_URL=https://pim.example.com

# Optional. Public artifact links, on a hostname of their own, not under the first one's cookies
# (another registrable domain is best). The proxy routes only its /p/* and /artifact-runtime/*.
# PIM_CONTENT_ORIGIN=https://pim-content.example.net

# Who may join once there is an admin: invite (default), open or closed.
# PIM_REGISTRATION=invite
# PIM_MAX_ACCOUNTS=10
# PIM_TIME_ZONE=Europe/Lisbon
# PIM_APPROVAL_POLICY=majordomo

# Members' limits (the admin has none). Unset is no limit.
# PIM_LIMIT_DAILY_TOKENS=2000000
# PIM_LIMIT_DAILY_RUNS=300

# Sign-in with your own OpenID Connect provider (Authentik, Keycloak, Pocket ID...): the issuer
# and button name here, the client's ID and secret in secrets.env. Not checked on celld yet
# (docs/celld.md, "Not verified").
# PIM_OIDC_ISSUER=https://auth.example.com
# PIM_OIDC_NAME=Authentik

# Traces to your own OTLP collector (docs/reference.md, Traces); its auth headers are a secret.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:4318

# Not set here, on purpose:
#   PIM_MODEL, PIM_MODELS, PIM_MEMORY_MODEL: Workers AI models. celld has none; the admin adds a
#     model provider in Settings → Model → Providers instead (docs/celld.md, "Models").
#   PIM_UTILITY_MODEL, PIM_IMAGE_MODEL: `off` in deploy/celld/wrangler.jsonc, for the same reason.
#   PIM_EMAIL_FROM: celld has no Email Workers, so Pim sends no email.
#   PIM_RUNTIME: `celld` in deploy/celld/wrangler.jsonc, for every celld Pim; deploy.sh refuses it here.
#   PIM_INGRESS_SECRET: a file of its own, which Caddy reads too (gen-ingress-secret.sh).
